  "x-qmanDigestDomain": "QMAN-DIRECTPATH/AER-VERIFIER-ALGORITHM/V1\u0000",
  "x-qmanDigestRule": "Deep-copy the complete schema-valid algorithm, set algorithmDigest to null only in the construction projection, encode it with CANONICAL-JSON-V1, prepend the exact x-qmanDigestDomain bytes, and SHA-256 the result.",
  "x-qmanStageRule": "Stages are ordered and fail closed. Exact built-in bytes are required for every caller document; raw byte, lexical node, depth, per-string, and aggregate-string limits are applied before constructing a JSON tree; duplicate-key-safe parsing is followed by a second exact tree-budget pass. Every fixed schema, generator, and conformance-test file is read exactly once into one immutable, exact-path source snapshot; all later schema parsing, hashing, algorithm construction, golden replay, and receipt contract checks consume only that snapshot and may not reopen a fixed path. The verifier then validates the complete fixed matrix/algorithm/golden bundle, every schema/raw-file/digest binding and receipt child itself. It must neither call nor import the target implementation as expected truth.",
  "x-qmanExactCoverageRule": "M24-M29 means the exact 133 ordered tuple rows in the bound matrix, never a generated Cartesian claim, subset, representative sample, or count-only assertion.",
  "x-qmanAuthorityBoundary": "COMPONENT_PREMISE",
  "x-qmanProductAuthorized": false,
  "x-qmanArtifactAuthorityBoundary": "The V1 candidate has no normative trusted artifact-resolver or typed authority-receipt interface. A successful run returns only STRUCTURALLY_VALID and componentEligible false; arbitrary digest strings or caller labels cannot promote it.",
  "x-qmanE4Boundary": "Successful execution proves only structural consistency. Component eligibility, E4, physical provenance, product Case closure, and product admission require separate independently governed artifacts."
}
